# tests/winterfest/wf_scenario_generic.expect
#
# The same scenario as wf_scenario.expect, run against a map that has NO rows in
# winterfest.ini's [presents]: fy_snow (a light map with player spawns and no
# generated present rows).
#
#   ./scripts/test-plugin.sh /path/to/tests/winterfest/wf_scenario.sma \
#       --profile freenova --bots 1 --map fy_snow \
#       --expect /path/to/tests/winterfest/wf_scenario_generic.expect
#
# What this proves that the dust2 run cannot: the generic '*' fallback really is
# used when a map has no entry of its own, and it resolves to `@t`/`@ct` spawn
# references rather than to nothing.

\[WF-TEST\] PASS season-open
\[WF-TEST\] PASS reset-clean
\[WF-TEST\] PASS gb-add
\[WF-TEST\] PASS grant-once
\[WF-TEST\] PASS grant-second-key
\[WF-TEST\] PASS gb-legacy-alias
\[WF-TEST\] PASS spins-consume
\[WF-TEST\] PASS pass-natives
\[WF-TEST\] PASS ornament-once
\[WF-TEST\] PASS tree-slot
\[WF-TEST\] PASS tree-slot-refused
\[WF-TEST\] PASS tree-clear
\[WF-TEST\] PASS visual-data
\[WF-TEST\] PASS visual-model-gated
\[WF-TEST\] PASS gift-once
\[WF-TEST\] PASS gift-instance
\[WF-TEST\] PASS open-once
\[WF-TEST\] PASS open-second-pays
\[WF-TEST\] PASS advent-today
\[WF-TEST\] PASS advent-late
\[WF-TEST\] PASS advent-locked
\[WF-TEST\] PASS pass-xp
\[WF-TEST\] summary pass=[0-9]+ fail=0

\[WF\] config: 3 rarities, 30 ornaments, 6 sets, 24 advent days, 30 pass tiers
\[WF\] spins: enabled, [0-9]+ free per day
\[WF\] daily spin granted to id [0-9]+
\[WF\] [0-9]+ visual id\(s\) configured, 6 prop slot\(s\) bound \(models gated

# The documented rule: a map with no rows of its own gets the generic set, and
# the count still has to land inside 6-10 (the '*' block is 8).
\[WF-GIFTS\] [0-9]+ present spot\(s\) on fy_snow from generic \* rows - ok \(rule: 6-10, default 8\)
\[WF-GIFTS\] season is closed - [0-9]+ spot\(s\) parsed, not spawned
\[WF-GIFTS\] spawned [0-9]+/[0-9]+ present glow\(s\)

\[WF\] admin [0-9]+ gave .* what=snowflakes .*code 1
\[WF\] admin [0-9]+ reloaded .*winterfest\.ini
\[WF-GIFTS\] player spawns on fy_snow

!\[WF-TEST\] FAIL
!Run time error
!bad load
